cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or dataset, please cite the article below.
title: "A model-free ceiling for vision-language model evaluation on rendered crystal structures"
abstract: >-
  A vision-language model that misreads a rendered crystal structure and one that misreasons about it
  produce the same wrong answer. When a benchmark is built by rendering a structure whose coordinates are
  known, no model is needed to separate them: inverting the known cameras and re-solving cross-view
  correspondence returns the answer the images support, a quantity we call the render ceiling.
type: software
